# LTX visual language

Follow `docs/LTX-MINI-SITE-GOALS.md`, `STYLE-GUIDE.md`, and `design/ltx.css`. This is a mini-website (`.site-section`), not a slide deck. Source is the LoRA training guide, not `sales-deck-original/`.

- Colors are the Webflow "LTX brand colors" set in `design/ltx.css`. Page ground is `--ltx-offwhite` (`#e7e8eb`). Ink is `--ltx-black` (`#0b0b0b`). No pink, green, or pure-white canvas. Accents are `--ltx-slate-dark` (current position) and `--ltx-slate-medium` (progress so far), on progress and position marks only. No purple. Active states are black.
- Aeonik, then Inter. Display through H3 is weight 400. H4–H6 and active labels are 500. Do not use 700, 800, or 900.
- Reuse Webflow class names: `heading-style-h*`, `h1-display`, `text-size-*`, `section-name-new` (eyebrow), `ltx-but-base` / `.is-black`. Do not invent a one-off style for a single element.
- In the sales deck, use `--fs-*` clamps and Webflow classes on every slide (no per-slide-type `--fs-*-stage` overrides). `--fs-*-stage` is only for a literal 1920×1080 canvas with no slide transform.
- Hairlines are 1px `--color-border`. Footage sits in `.media-card` with `--scrim`.
- Index numbers are zero-padded, `tabular-nums`, in a `--nav-num-col` track.
- Motion uses `--ease-out-soft` and the transition tokens. Honor `prefers-reduced-motion`. In-page links jump; they do not smooth-scroll.
- Leave `sales-deck-original/` as reference. New slides link `design/ltx.css`.

```css
/* ❌ scaled slide title */
.title { font-size: 70px; font-weight: 600; color: #111; }

/* ✅ deck title */
.title { font-size: var(--fs-h1); font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: var(--ls-h1); color: var(--color-ink); }
```
